  "description": "The face. Over the forehead, the nose and the chin bone lies within about a centimetre of the skin. The eyeballs sit in the orbits behind thin eyelids: between the eyeball and the infraorbital margin (ST1, EX-HN7) and beside the inner canthus against the medial orbital wall (BL1) a needle runs into the orbital fat a few millimetres from the eyeball, and the optic nerve and ophthalmic vessels lie at the apex of the orbit a few centimetres behind the rim; bleeding into the orbit is the common complication. The supratrochlear and supraorbital nerves leave the orbit under the medial and middle parts of the eyebrow and run up the forehead; the infraorbital nerve emerges from its foramen below the orbit (ST2). The facial artery runs up from the jaw lateral to the corner of the mouth and along the nasolabial sulcus, and continues as the angular artery beside the nose to the inner canthus. The lips and the cheek beside the corner of the mouth lead into the mouth. The temple lies over the temporalis and its fascia.",
